# Citation File Format 1.2.0 — https://citation-file-format.github.io
# How to cite this work. Read by GitHub, Zenodo and reference managers.
#
# TO BE FILLED BY THE OWNER at the 1.0.0 release, and not before:
#   doi:           the Zenodo DOI of the deposit, e.g. 10.5281/zenodo.0000000
#   version:       1.0.0
#   date-released: the release date, YYYY-MM-DD
# Each is left out rather than guessed: nothing is released yet, and a citation
# that names a DOI which does not resolve is worse than one that names none.
#
# Written with AI assistance, reviewed and published by a person. (CFF 1.2.0 has no
# note field and allows no extra key, so this sentence lives in a comment.)
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: If you use this software or specification, please cite it as below.
title: "AgenticSystemCore: a format for publishing machine-discoverable knowledge"
abstract: >-
  A specification and reference implementation for publishing knowledge as
  Markdown bundles that compile to a static site, an RDF graph, agent skills and
  machine-readable discovery documents, so that both people and software agents
  can find, read and cite the same material with its provenance intact.
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Besleaga
    given-names: Andrei N.
    orcid: https://orcid.org/0009-0001-3464-5283
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: https://github.com/andreibesleaga/agentic-system-core
url: https://agenticsystemcore.com
keywords:
  - knowledge representation
  - agentic systems
  - provenance
  - linked data
  - static site
  - specification
